  "latest_findings": {
    "integrated_run": "RUN-006 numerically launched the current Mode A architecture for 6 h using the literature-grounded 21.2109 m2 POMS crown, coreless AFPM, dual battery, explicit hydrogen fuel boundary and the current calcium-maintenance architecture.",
    "screening_schedule": "0.5 h prime at 12 W auxiliaries, 4 h linear PEMFC ramp at 10 W auxiliaries, then 1.5 h hold at 8 W auxiliaries. These are screening assumptions, not hardware measurements.",
    "nominal_0p130_empirical": "At 0.130 mg/m2/s and the RUN005 empirical conversion, steady net is +2.3403 W but total dual-pack energy is still -23.3195 Wh after 6 h; startup repayment occurs around 16.49 h if the modeled steady state persists.",
    "nominal_0p130_design": "At the same flux and 55% design conversion, total pack energy returns to the initial level around 4.09 h and ends the 6 h screen about +33.03 Wh after 95% bidirectional DC/DC efficiencies.",
    "matrix_result": "In the 55% design branch the six-hour battery-neutral screen passes from 0.100 mg/m2/s upward. The empirical branch needs higher flux and/or longer hold; 0.160-0.1707 mg/m2/s repay startup around 9.34-8.28 h in this model.",
    "fuel_boundary": "At the nominal 0.130 mg/m2/s six-hour trajectory the model transports about 34.74 g O2 and requires about 4.38 g stoichiometric H2 minimum. Hydrogen remains the external primary chemical-energy source.",
    "regen_boundary": "No AFPM regenerative power is credited in RUN-006 because no independent hydraulic/mechanical source has yet been measured."
